NOTICE: bundled Short form list sources (revision sf05-fixture-1)

The app's generated Short forms draw on word shortenings and acronyms built from
these sources by scripts/abbreviation-lists/. Neither src/ nor crates/ contains
networking code; the lists reach the app only through the versioned snapshot.

1. O*NET Database 31.0, U.S. Department of Labor, Employment and Training
   Administration (USDOL/ETA). English role titles and acronyms.
   License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ .
   Source: https://www.onetcenter.org/database.html (db_31_0_json/job_titles.json).
   Changes: kept rows with a parenthesised short form; gated (first letter,
   letter order, shorter, whole-word) with drop counts in build-report.json.

2. Wiktionary via kaikki.org (English and Spanish extractions). Word shortenings.
   The derived data file is shared alike: Creative Commons
   Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0),
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ (Wiktionary text is CC BY-SA
   4.0 and GFDL: https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wiktionary:Copyrights).
   Source: https://kaikki.org/dictionary/rawdata.html (pins in README.md).
   Changes: kept abbreviation/acronym/initialism senses with one target;
   gated as above with drop counts in build-report.json.

3. Wikidata concept entities (per-item revision ids in the build inputs).
   License: CC0 1.0 Universal, https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/ .
   Source: https://www.wikidata.org/ . Changes: P1813 short names and
   abbreviation-shaped aliases of the concept list the script defines.

